SUMMARY:Deadline: LawAI Summer Research Fellowship (EU Law) 2027\, Cambridg
 e UK (GBP 1\,000 a week)
DESCRIPTION:A paid summer of mentored research on how EU law governs advanc
 ed AI\, including the AI Act and its enforcement\, working with the Instit
 ute for Law & AI's team in Cambridge. WHO: people with a legal background\
 , from students to academics and practitioners\; prior AI experience is no
 t required\, and the organisers note that strong candidates often underrat
 e their fit.\n\nOrganisation: Institute for Law & AI (LawAI)\nLocation: Ca
 mbridge\, UK\, in person preferred\; other arrangements considered case by
  case.\nAward: GBP 1\,000 weekly stipend\, plus a GBP 7\,000 relocation pa
 yment for fellows who move to Cambridge for the full fellowship. No applic
 ation fee mentioned.\nDuration: 10 weeks in summer 2027.\n\nMore: https://
 law-ai.org/srf-eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://law-ai.org/srf-eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
LOCATION:Cambridge\, UK\, in person preferred\; other arrangements consider
 ed case by case.
END:VEVENT
