SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 EST: LawAI Summer Research Fellowship (Legal Frontie
 rs) 2027 (USD 1\,800 or GBP 1\,000 a week\, remote-first)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 29 Jan 2027 at 23:59 EST.\n\nA paid summer research fell
 owship on frontier questions in law and AI\, such as AI systems that follo
 w the law and what automated governance means for the rule of law. Fellows
  are mentored by the Institute for Law & AI's researchers and produce a pi
 ece of research. WHO: law students\, legal professionals and academics\; i
 nterdisciplinary approaches are welcome.\n\nOrganisation: Institute for La
 w & AI (LawAI)\nLocation: Remote-first\, with optional in-person work in C
 ambridge\, UK or Washington\, DC. Fellows need work permission for the pla
 ce they will be based.\nAward: Weekly subsidy by location: USD 1\,800 a we
 ek for fellows based in the US\, GBP 1\,000 a week for fellows based in th
 e EU or UK. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: 10 weeks in summer 20
 27.\n\nMore: https://law-ai.org/srf-lf/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://law-ai.org/srf-lf/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
LOCATION:Remote-first\, with optional in-person work in Cambridge\, UK or W
 ashington\, DC. Fellows need work permission for the place they will be ba
 sed.
